            "id": "21255298",
            "user": "Flickety",
            "timestamp": "19:46, 31 October 2016",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(8,447 bytes)",
            "change": -47,
            "summary": "(Switch to appropriate category)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "Converting your attic into usable finished space can increase the value of your home by maximizing the available square footage. If your home is smaller than other homes in your area, or simply lacks the necessary amount of storage or living space for your family, finishing your attic is a relatively inexpensive way to increase your usable space. You can learn the proper code specifications and plan to insulate and wire your attic for better purposes than storage.",
                    "",
                    "[[Category:Attics and Lofts]]",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "Converting your attic into usable finished space can increase the value of your home by maximizing the available square footage. If your home is smaller than other homes in your area, or simply lacks the necessary amount of storage or living space for your family, finishing your attic is a relatively inexpensive way to increase your usable space. You can learn the proper code specifications and plan to insulate and wire your attic for better purposes than storage. See Step 1 for more information.",
                    "[[Category:Build Design & Remodel Own Home]]"
                ]
            }
        },
