            "contribution_type": "cleanup",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Check the ceiling height. For a finished attic to be to code, it must satisfy the same living requirements of other rooms, sometimes called the \"rule of sevens.\" Any living space in a home needs to have at least {{convert|7|ft|m|1}} of clearance from the floor to the ceiling, and there needs to be at least 70 square feet of space available, at least {{convert|7|ft|m|1}} in each direction. At least 50 percent of the attic space must have {{convert|7|ft|m|adj=on|1}} clearance.<ref>http://www.thisoldhouse.com/toh/article/0,,20267119,00.html</ref> [[Image:1537145 1.jpg|center|416px]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Check the ceiling height. For an finished attic to be to code, it must satisfy the same living requirements of other rooms, sometimes called the \"rule of sevens.\" Any living space in a home needs to have at least {{convert|7|ft|m|1}} of clearance from the floor to the ceiling, and there needs to be at least 70 square feet of space available, at least {{convert|7|ft|m|1}} in each direction. At least 50 percent of the attic space must have {{convert|7|ft|m|adj=on|1}} clearance.<ref>http://www.thisoldhouse.com/toh/article/0,,20267119,00.html</ref> [[Image:1537145 1.jpg|center|416px]]"
                ]
