            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "Converting your attic into usable finished space increases the value of your home by maximizing the available square footage. If your home is smaller than other homes in your area, or simply lacks the necessary amount of storage or living space for your family, finishing your attic is a relatively inexpensive way to increase your usable space.",
                    "# [[Image:Finish an Attic Step 1.jpg|right|300px]]Remove any existing loose or blown insulation in the attic. Use a builders vacuum to get all of the small pieces. Consider renting a commercial air purifier for the duration of the project to minimize the possibility of inhaling the tiny insulation strands.",
